@title Cabinet: drag a duct's end handle shorter, then cut it to a stock length (1920x1080)
@area Cabinet
@sizes 1920x1080
# Rails and ducts window (palette: rails): Add duct selects the new duct, with its two end handles on the plate and
# its length and bar in the card at the top of the window. The finish handle is dragged left (the label shows the
# new length), the duct stays put at its start; Cut to length offers the stock lengths; Ctrl+Z undoes each step.
open qa/fixtures/cabinet-lesson.novo
wait 20
click_text Cabinet #1
wait 30
key ctrl+k
wait 3
text rails and ducts
wait 4
key Enter
wait 10
click_text "Add duct"
wait 10
expect "Cut from one 2000 mm bar"
expect "Trim at point"
shot card
mouse_down 1499 1008
move 1439 1008
move 1379 1008
wait 5
shot dragging
mouse_up 1379 1008
wait 10
expect "Cut from one 2000 mm bar"
shot shortened
check_layout
key ctrl+z
wait 10
shot undone
click_text "Cut to length"
wait 5
shot cut-menu
